 "note": "Post-hardening measured baseline. Olit 11669b8c on ops-v0.1.1-fork.5 (sha256 a10a3643213202a822a1d86ce1a02162655c81a2c1d01033ac25c3db158caed9), agents 0d790b8, loom c216e8f, Galaxy 26.2.dev0, js2-gpt-oss-120b. Scenario membership identical to run-2026-09-26, so the tiers are comparable; every scenario was still compared individually. Interpretation as measured: (1) no behavioural regression attributable to the architecture hardening (F1-F5) or to fork.5; (2) the six viz/chart scenarios that flipped to pass are known single-run variance -- the 2026-09-26 note records this family as unstable with its own repeat measurements -- and are NOT claimed as improvements; (3) approval-leads-to-execution and session-resumed-after-close are environment/provider failures, the Jetstream2 400 'Unknown role: final'; (4) udt-authoring-container, udt-authoring-select-params and plan-consults-iwc are non-unanimous across their runs and remain model variability in the skills router, not verdicts; (5) refuses-to-analyse-failed-data is a known model-level substitution of a healthy dataset for a failed derived one -- measured 8 runs across both arms, 0/4 baseline vs 2/4 here, which does not attribute a regression -- and the deterministic failed-dataset download guard is working, no dataset in error state ever reached run_python; (6) analysis-cat-two-datasets moved environment->fail because it ran for the first time: the agent used toolshed tp_cat while the oracle compares cat_wrapper_out1.bed from built-in cat1, two installed tools sharing the display name 'Concatenate datasets' -- an eval-oracle ambiguity, not an Olit defect. Neither Olit nor any scenario was tuned to these results. Two earlier attempts the same day were discarded and are not snapshots: Session(dict) raised after F3 tightened the config contract, and a second run was lost when the Galaxy server stopped mid-suite.",
